            <ArticleTitle>Colonoscopic Splenic Injury: A Simplified Radiologic Approach.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2615453</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1155/2016/2615453</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Colonoscopy is a commonly performed procedure for diagnosis and treatment of large bowel diseases. Recognized complications include bleeding and perforation. Splenic injury during colonoscopy is a rare complication. We report a case of a 73-year-old woman who presented with left-sided abdominal pain after colonoscopy with finding of splenic injury on CT scan. She was managed conservatively. We discuss the diagnostic and therapeutic approach to colonoscopic splenic injury.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
